      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining File Structure**\n\nI'm solidifying the need for a `stream_platform_generation.py` file in Python. My focus is now on how to best structure this file. I'm exploring methods to preserve provider response objects during the streaming process and also ensuring there's a clear way to identify the chosen external provider within the code.\n\n\n**Structuring the Implementation**\n\nNow I'm focusing on the implementation of `stream_platform_generation.py`. I'm going to leverage the Vertex AI Python SDK, starting with `google.cloud.aiplatform`. I'm planning a function, perhaps called `stream_gemini_output`, taking a prompt and model config. It will initialize a `GenerativeModel` client for the streaming and preserve those raw response objects from the provider.\n\n\n**Defining the Core Function**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the function's core within `stream_platform_generation.py`. I've decided it should be called `stream_gemini_output`. I'll implement it to take a prompt and configuration. The function will initialize a `GenerativeModel` client and call `generate_content` with streaming enabled. It's crucial this preserves the Vertex AI response objects directly. I'll need to research the exact Vertex AI SDK methods, and how the generator works.\n\n\n",
